1
00:01:30,530 --> 00:01:34,979
[AWAKEN]

2
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:37,930
[Episode 4]

3
00:01:42,070 --> 00:01:42,870
Inspector Su,

4
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:44,180
any instructions?

5
00:01:44,350 --> 00:01:46,200
I'll speak to
Director Li personally tomorrow.

6
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:47,259
That would be best.

7
00:02:04,790 --> 00:02:05,480
Hello.

8
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:06,840
Director, it's me.

9
00:02:08,030 --> 00:02:09,430
Do you have any idea what time it is?

10
00:02:09,430 --> 00:02:11,090
Can't it wait until tomorrow?

11
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,190
Su Men suddenly decided to
interrogate that Chen guy.

12
00:02:14,190 --> 00:02:15,430
I don't know what she asked him.

13
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:17,829
She said she'd
tell you in person tomorrow.

14
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:20,190
This woman is such a nuisance.

15
00:02:21,090 --> 00:02:22,420
Doesn't she ever sleep?

16
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:27,710
Is the confession ready?

17
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:30,050
Yes. All the paperwork is in order.

18
00:02:30,510 --> 00:02:32,630
Have him executed along with
tomorrow morning's first batch.

19
00:02:32,630 --> 00:02:34,400
Once it's taken care of, I'll go see her.

20
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:35,710
Better not leave room for complications.

21
00:02:35,710 --> 00:02:36,440
Understood.

22
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:14,310
For you.

23
00:03:15,630 --> 00:03:16,490
Flowers again?

24
00:03:17,360 --> 00:03:18,760
Aren't you tired of this?

25
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:25,340
Do you happen to have 5,000 yuan?

26
00:03:25,710 --> 00:03:26,430
I do.

27
00:03:26,980 --> 00:03:27,630
Good.

28
00:03:27,980 --> 00:03:29,710
Then drive me to the Paramount.

29
00:03:29,820 --> 00:03:30,910
The Paramount?

30
00:03:39,829 --> 00:03:42,470
[In January 1942, I borrowed 5,000 yuan
from Young Master Feng—Jinbao]

31
00:03:43,670 --> 00:03:45,760
Actually, you don't need to
write me an IOU.

32
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:47,890
It's not that I can't spare 5,000 yuan.

33
00:03:48,820 --> 00:03:50,150
You giving it to me is one thing—

34
00:03:50,150 --> 00:03:52,150
my borrowing it from you is another.

35
00:03:52,260 --> 00:03:54,670
Even close brothers
should keep accounts straight.

36
00:03:54,670 --> 00:03:57,020
Could you come to
Chongqing with me and settle down?

37
00:03:57,020 --> 00:03:58,910
We could open a small match factory

38
00:03:58,910 --> 00:04:00,170
and live a simple life.

39
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:07,760
Who says I want to
live a simple life with you?

40
00:04:08,330 --> 00:04:10,330
Chongqing? I've never been there.

41
00:04:11,390 --> 00:04:12,720
Is it as big as Shanghai?

42
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:22,390
You're Shasha?

43
00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:23,870
I'm Jinbao.

44
00:04:24,750 --> 00:04:26,550
Give the flowers to Miss Shasha.

45
00:04:27,050 --> 00:04:29,830
[Shasha, Dance Hall Girl]

46
00:04:28,420 --> 00:04:30,150
What kind of character are you?

47
00:04:30,310 --> 00:04:31,430
He's no "character."

48
00:04:31,430 --> 00:04:32,630
He's Young Master Feng.

49
00:04:32,630 --> 00:04:34,630
I stole him from Bingbing.

50
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:37,900
Like Bingbing,

51
00:04:37,970 --> 00:04:39,140
I'm also with MGM.

52
00:04:45,990 --> 00:04:47,340
You should've seen the look

53
00:04:47,340 --> 00:04:48,990
on Bingbing's face that day.

54
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:50,460
Her expression

55
00:04:50,510 --> 00:04:52,390
was as sour as spoiled soup.

56
00:04:58,460 --> 00:05:00,510
That bitch finally got
what was coming to her.

57
00:05:00,510 --> 00:05:02,360
Back when I worked at MGM,

58
00:05:02,390 --> 00:05:03,850
she gave me no end of grief.

59
00:05:04,140 --> 00:05:05,870
We're both women fallen on hard times.

60
00:05:05,870 --> 00:05:07,310
I'm sure we'll become good sisters.

61
00:05:07,310 --> 00:05:09,510
Come on. I'll buy you a late-night meal.

62
00:05:12,330 --> 00:05:13,570
I, Zhu Dahei,

63
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:15,800
hereby become
sworn sisters with you, Jinbao.

64
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,550
We may not be born on the same day,

65
00:05:17,550 --> 00:05:19,430
but we shall die on the same day.

66
00:05:19,660 --> 00:05:20,660
Die? No way.

67
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:22,510
I want us both to live forever—

68
00:05:22,540 --> 00:05:23,540
let's be fairies.

69
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:25,340
Okay.

70
00:05:34,310 --> 00:05:35,870
Flowers—for the fairy.

71
00:05:36,170 --> 00:05:37,970
Money—for Captain Cang.

72
00:05:44,630 --> 00:05:46,230
You have a friend in trouble?

73
00:05:49,210 --> 00:05:50,290
It's my lover.

74
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:54,150
Drink.

75
00:05:55,950 --> 00:05:56,550
Alright.

76
00:06:24,410 --> 00:06:25,410
Inspector Su.

77
00:06:26,660 --> 00:06:27,550
Captain Cang.

78
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:30,190
In such a rush to execute him?

79
00:06:30,190 --> 00:06:31,990
I'm just carrying out my duties.

80
00:06:32,070 --> 00:06:33,330
Who gave you the order?

81
00:06:38,310 --> 00:06:40,430
I'm acting according to regulations.

82
00:06:40,430 --> 00:06:41,760
Here is his confession.

83
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:53,480
I'm the inspector overseeing this case.

84
00:06:53,780 --> 00:06:54,980
Without my approval,

85
00:06:55,510 --> 00:06:56,950
no one shall execute him.

86
00:07:09,510 --> 00:07:11,110
An outsider with no background at all

87
00:07:11,110 --> 00:07:13,570
is actually the one
who killed Yu Yingxiang?

88
00:07:13,990 --> 00:07:14,780
Director Li,

89
00:07:15,390 --> 00:07:17,120
do you accept that conclusion?

90
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:22,360
But he's the only suspect.

91
00:07:28,630 --> 00:07:31,030
The motive for the murder
was simply money.

92
00:07:34,659 --> 00:07:37,510
Yu Yingxiang's collusion with the NBIS
is a major case.

93
00:07:37,510 --> 00:07:38,460
Yet you're putting on

94
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:41,260
this coerced-confession act
right in front of me?

95
00:07:41,310 --> 00:07:43,390
Even if Yu Yingxiang had been captured,

96
00:07:43,390 --> 00:07:44,950
he'd have been executed anyway.

97
00:07:44,950 --> 00:07:47,140
At least he got an easy death.

98
00:07:48,110 --> 00:07:49,140
This case

99
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:50,950
has to be brought to an end eventually.

100
00:07:50,950 --> 00:07:53,810
The Japanese are
still waiting for an explanation.

101
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:56,090
The Japanese aren't fools.

102
00:07:56,770 --> 00:07:58,370
If you hand them this result,

103
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:01,550
they'll only think
you're brushing them off.

104
00:08:02,510 --> 00:08:03,770
Then, in your opinion,

105
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:06,630
if that guy is not the one who did it,

106
00:08:06,700 --> 00:08:08,190
how did Yu Yingxiang die?

107
00:08:10,780 --> 00:08:11,780
Could he have

108
00:08:12,220 --> 00:08:14,550
committed suicide to escape punishment?

109
00:08:20,990 --> 00:08:21,750
Suicide?

110
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:28,100
Suicide would actually hold up.

111
00:08:32,539 --> 00:08:33,350
Understood.

112
00:08:35,470 --> 00:08:37,299
Then, what about that guy?

113
00:08:38,830 --> 00:08:40,830
That guy has nothing to do with this.

114
00:08:41,390 --> 00:08:42,720
You and I both know that.

115
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:46,140
Alright.

116
00:08:47,430 --> 00:08:49,630
Then we will do as you say, Inspector Su.

117
00:08:50,900 --> 00:08:53,340
He committed suicide to escape punishment.

118
00:08:53,340 --> 00:08:54,940
That accounts for his death.

119
00:08:56,510 --> 00:08:58,230
What about the money he embezzled?

120
00:08:58,230 --> 00:08:59,430
Please rest assured.

121
00:08:59,870 --> 00:09:02,660
I'll recover every penny of the money

122
00:09:02,950 --> 00:09:04,300
Yu Yingxiang embezzled,

123
00:09:04,300 --> 00:09:06,700
so you'll have something proper to report.

124
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:12,110
I've heard you like green tea.

125
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:15,010
I've prepared some especially for you.

126
00:09:23,870 --> 00:09:25,390
Newspapers! Get your newspapers!

127
00:09:25,390 --> 00:09:27,320
Newspapers! Get your newspapers!

128
00:09:29,730 --> 00:09:32,260
Yu Yingxiang's case
is closed just like that?

129
00:09:33,390 --> 00:09:34,990
Yu Yingxiang must've

130
00:09:34,990 --> 00:09:37,190
acted alone in colluding with the NBIS.

131
00:09:38,230 --> 00:09:40,040
Li Moqun had him eliminated

132
00:09:40,070 --> 00:09:41,600
to cover up the corruption.

133
00:09:42,870 --> 00:09:44,530
We'll never find that killer.

134
00:09:45,420 --> 00:09:48,420
And even if we did,
we wouldn't get anything out of him.

135
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:52,400
There's no need to
make Chen Kailai the scapegoat for this.

136
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:55,260
Chen Kailai is quite unlucky.

137
00:09:57,990 --> 00:09:59,140
How did he manage to survive

138
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:01,350
the interrogation at No. 76?

139
00:10:05,620 --> 00:10:07,220
Can you release Chen Kailai?

140
00:10:07,790 --> 00:10:09,320
He's an innocent civilian.

141
00:10:10,110 --> 00:10:11,180
I've been busy all night.

142
00:10:11,180 --> 00:10:12,870
I just wanted to get some good sleep.

143
00:10:12,870 --> 00:10:14,730
Let's talk about it another time.

144
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:16,660
Important matters

145
00:10:16,830 --> 00:10:19,030
should be raised at the important time.

146
00:10:19,390 --> 00:10:20,260
Besides,

147
00:10:20,550 --> 00:10:23,300
you came back to sleep,
and yet you still want to do this?

148
00:10:23,300 --> 00:10:25,110
I just wanted to sleep better.

149
00:10:27,660 --> 00:10:29,230
I already promised my sworn sister

150
00:10:29,230 --> 00:10:30,490
I'd intercede for him.

151
00:10:34,470 --> 00:10:36,260
None of you women are any good!

152
00:10:40,630 --> 00:10:42,230
Chen Kailai cannot be released.

153
00:10:42,230 --> 00:10:43,180
That's an order.

154
00:10:45,060 --> 00:10:46,790
I've already taken the money.

155
00:10:47,170 --> 00:10:48,270
Think of something.

156
00:10:48,270 --> 00:10:49,470
Then give the money back!

157
00:10:49,470 --> 00:10:50,400
I'm telling you,

158
00:10:51,260 --> 00:10:53,020
no one can save Chen Kailai.

159
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:58,180
How come you were able to release
all those other people before?

160
00:10:58,180 --> 00:10:59,900
Useless thing.

161
00:10:59,900 --> 00:11:01,830
All you ever do is crawl into my bed.

162
00:11:10,590 --> 00:11:11,180
Hello?

163
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:12,660
Come back immediately

164
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:14,340
and release Chen Kailai.

165
00:11:16,390 --> 00:11:16,990
Yes.

166
00:11:24,140 --> 00:11:26,740
She's my best sworn sister.

167
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:47,140
Alright, alright.

168
00:11:47,940 --> 00:11:49,340
There, there. Don't cry.

169
00:11:53,390 --> 00:11:54,190
Let me ask you.

170
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:56,670
How much did your sworn sister

171
00:11:56,670 --> 00:11:57,460
give you?

172
00:12:01,060 --> 00:12:01,940
Four thousand.

173
00:12:05,510 --> 00:12:07,060
Four thousand's a bit low.

174
00:12:10,510 --> 00:12:11,770
Let me see what I can do.

175
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:15,390
Cang,

176
00:12:15,660 --> 00:12:17,060
you really are a good man.

177
00:12:36,940 --> 00:12:38,590
The latest German model.

178
00:12:42,940 --> 00:12:44,490
It's a waste in my hands.

179
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:53,760
Could you take a photograph of me?

180
00:13:00,940 --> 00:13:01,830
Here's fine.

181
00:13:06,260 --> 00:13:06,780
Okay.

182
00:13:33,180 --> 00:13:34,980
"Justice for all under heaven."

183
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:41,070
Is there any justice here?

184
00:13:48,540 --> 00:13:50,000
Let me take you home first.

185
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:23,710
I know.

186
00:14:24,630 --> 00:14:26,940
If it weren't for her,
I wouldn't be out today.

187
00:14:26,940 --> 00:14:28,780
It's hard to survive in Shanghai.

188
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:30,440
Connections are everything.

189
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:12,960
You really don't know
who killed Yu Yingxiang?

190
00:15:22,180 --> 00:15:22,830
General,

191
00:15:23,590 --> 00:15:26,470
why do you think
Yu Yingxiang wanted so much money?

192
00:15:27,350 --> 00:15:28,480
A man only needs food

193
00:15:28,710 --> 00:15:30,710
and a roof over his head in this life.

194
00:15:31,110 --> 00:15:33,900
All that money—you can't take it along
when you die, nor spend it all while alive.

195
00:15:33,900 --> 00:15:36,350
And in the end, he died by his own hand.

196
00:15:42,780 --> 00:15:44,390
Money is still necessary.

197
00:15:46,540 --> 00:15:48,750
But greed, anger, and ignorance

198
00:15:50,390 --> 00:15:51,990
are the great taboos of life.

199
00:15:52,780 --> 00:15:54,040
And greed is the worst.

200
00:16:06,390 --> 00:16:07,300
Director Li,

201
00:16:08,510 --> 00:16:11,140
this matter was handled a bit hastily.

202
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:13,780
Yes, General.

203
00:16:14,420 --> 00:16:15,390
We did

204
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:18,350
handle this matter rather hastily.

205
00:16:23,140 --> 00:16:25,750
And regarding Yu Yingxiang's leaking
of information

206
00:16:25,750 --> 00:16:27,420
that got Mr. Suzuki killed in Hangzhou,

207
00:16:27,420 --> 00:16:29,220
and his collusion with the NBIS—

208
00:16:30,750 --> 00:16:33,210
shouldn't we investigate that thoroughly?

209
00:16:34,990 --> 00:16:36,650
Since the man is already dead,

210
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:38,920
the matter can only stand as it is.

211
00:16:39,750 --> 00:16:42,140
I just wonder
whether he had any accomplices

212
00:16:42,140 --> 00:16:43,420
within No. 76.

213
00:16:44,350 --> 00:16:46,550
This is a serious threat to Director Li.

214
00:16:48,350 --> 00:16:49,950
It's also kept me up at night.

215
00:17:01,180 --> 00:17:03,350
Make a few extra dishes tonight.

216
00:17:04,579 --> 00:17:05,780
Yangzhou fried rice,

217
00:17:06,069 --> 00:17:07,589
stir-fried shredded pork
with winter bamboo shoots,

218
00:17:07,589 --> 00:17:10,190
and stir-fried cabbage
with water chestnuts!

219
00:17:10,630 --> 00:17:12,560
Every blind man can tell fortunes.

220
00:17:13,069 --> 00:17:15,900
Tonight we're welcoming my disciple back!

221
00:17:29,940 --> 00:17:31,900
We still need to make fried tofu puffs.

222
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:33,310
Aside from Yangzhou fried rice,

223
00:17:33,310 --> 00:17:34,630
they're his favorite.

224
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:46,870
♪ A true gentleman
never forgets a kindness ♪

225
00:17:50,980 --> 00:17:51,660
Thank you.

226
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:52,590
You're welcome.

227
00:17:55,870 --> 00:17:58,590
♪ Ungrateful ♪

228
00:17:59,660 --> 00:18:01,790
The agency has received intelligence

229
00:18:02,420 --> 00:18:04,740
that the Communist operative
code-named Diana

230
00:18:04,740 --> 00:18:06,200
has begun to make her move.

231
00:18:07,270 --> 00:18:09,550
The NBIS's agent God of Wealth
has also been activated

232
00:18:09,550 --> 00:18:11,150
and has arrived in Shanghai.

233
00:18:11,940 --> 00:18:13,790
They must all be related

234
00:18:13,790 --> 00:18:15,630
to our Project Slumber.

235
00:18:17,270 --> 00:18:21,630
No. 76 is the security bureau
Mr. Wang trusts.

236
00:18:23,070 --> 00:18:24,310
You mustn't let

237
00:18:25,070 --> 00:18:27,200
what happened to Suzuki happen again.

238
00:18:27,830 --> 00:18:28,420
Yes.

239
00:18:30,070 --> 00:18:31,590
Why is Shanghai

240
00:18:31,590 --> 00:18:33,070
crawling with spies?

241
00:18:34,740 --> 00:18:36,110
Director Li, you've been
racking your brain over this.

242
00:18:36,110 --> 00:18:37,970
You must be feeling overwhelmed.

243
00:18:38,070 --> 00:18:39,180
You're not even that old,

244
00:18:39,180 --> 00:18:40,910
but you already have gray hair.

245
00:18:41,830 --> 00:18:45,490
Now corruption and collusion with the NBIS
are tangled together.

246
00:18:46,220 --> 00:18:46,940
General,

247
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:49,590
I should've taken up a post at No. 76

248
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:52,160
and started the investigation long ago.

249
00:18:54,310 --> 00:18:55,040
Director Li,

250
00:18:56,140 --> 00:18:57,500
I assume you have no objection

251
00:18:57,500 --> 00:19:00,350
to my helping you
root out the internal threats, right?

252
00:19:00,350 --> 00:19:01,150
Inspector Su,

253
00:19:01,870 --> 00:19:03,200
of course I support you.

254
00:19:03,230 --> 00:19:04,420
It's just that it's too chaotic

255
00:19:04,420 --> 00:19:06,420
and dangerous at No. 76.

256
00:19:08,030 --> 00:19:09,900
I was targeted for assassination
as soon as I got off the train.

257
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:12,230
They meant to stop me from investigating.

258
00:19:12,310 --> 00:19:13,110
Could No. 76

259
00:19:13,390 --> 00:19:14,650
be any more dangerous?

260
00:19:19,270 --> 00:19:22,660
I still have faith in
your abilities, Director Li.

261
00:19:24,700 --> 00:19:28,180
But now is a critical moment
for purging the traitors.

262
00:19:30,580 --> 00:19:33,850
Inspector Su, I hope you'll
take up a post at No. 76

263
00:19:34,460 --> 00:19:38,550
and assist Director Li in
carrying out this operation.

264
00:19:40,350 --> 00:19:42,220
Thank you for your trust, General.

265
00:19:42,220 --> 00:19:43,030
I agree.

266
00:19:44,140 --> 00:19:44,740
Good.

267
00:19:46,390 --> 00:19:49,140
I hope you two can work together

268
00:19:49,860 --> 00:19:53,230
and ensure Project Slumber
proceeds smoothly.

269
00:19:56,700 --> 00:19:58,460
Tell me—which kills faster,

270
00:19:59,700 --> 00:20:01,270
a bullet or a string?

271
00:20:05,270 --> 00:20:06,140
If you ask me,

272
00:20:07,250 --> 00:20:09,450
killing is wrong no matter how you do it.

273
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:11,500
Even killing traitors is wrong?

274
00:20:23,110 --> 00:20:24,570
Even Yeller knows that...

275
00:20:26,130 --> 00:20:27,320
the NBIS's Hurricane Team

276
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:31,180
is in Shanghai carrying out
Mr. Dai's mission to eliminate traitors.

277
00:20:37,790 --> 00:20:39,100
I'm just a blind man.

278
00:20:42,310 --> 00:20:43,140
Chen Kailai!

279
00:20:43,460 --> 00:20:44,350
Chen Kailai!

280
00:20:45,900 --> 00:20:46,900
Chen Kailai!

281
00:20:47,420 --> 00:20:48,350
Chen Kailai!

282
00:20:48,370 --> 00:20:49,130
I'm here.

283
00:20:51,110 --> 00:20:51,870
Let me see.

284
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:53,250
You're hurt.

285
00:20:53,280 --> 00:20:54,840
No, no, easy. Be gentle.

286
00:20:54,940 --> 00:20:56,200
I lost my fingernails.

287
00:20:57,070 --> 00:20:58,330
Then sit down quickly.

288
00:20:58,980 --> 00:21:00,710
Your whole face is injured too.

289
00:21:02,590 --> 00:21:03,860
I was so worried about you.

290
00:21:03,860 --> 00:21:05,310
Getting out of No. 76—

291
00:21:05,330 --> 00:21:07,870
that's practically like
returning to the land of the living.

292
00:21:07,870 --> 00:21:09,240
I didn't kill the man.

293
00:21:09,460 --> 00:21:11,120
Why wouldn't they release me?

294
00:21:11,180 --> 00:21:12,230
Those bastards

295
00:21:12,460 --> 00:21:14,230
don't need evidence to arrest people.

296
00:21:14,230 --> 00:21:15,650
If I hadn't pulled some strings,

297
00:21:15,650 --> 00:21:17,110
you'd have lost your life.

298
00:21:17,140 --> 00:21:18,340
Pulled some strings?

299
00:21:20,240 --> 00:21:22,040
This is my sworn sister, Shasha—

300
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:24,020
our bond runs deeper than the sea
and is stronger

301
00:21:24,020 --> 00:21:24,700
than gold.

302
00:21:26,040 --> 00:21:27,500
Jinbao's a real sucker for love.

303
00:21:27,500 --> 00:21:28,870
I'd never spend 5,000 yuan

304
00:21:28,870 --> 00:21:30,040
on any man.

305
00:21:30,950 --> 00:21:31,560
How much?

306
00:21:31,710 --> 00:21:33,910
Five thousand. You have to give me an IOU.

307
00:21:33,910 --> 00:21:34,840
Five thousand?

308
00:21:35,170 --> 00:21:35,970
Are you crazy?

309
00:21:36,430 --> 00:21:38,490
Who asked you to pay people off for me?

310
00:21:38,520 --> 00:21:39,540
Weren't you broke?

311
00:21:39,540 --> 00:21:40,800
Where did you get the 5,000?

312
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:41,690
Young Master Feng gave it to me.

313
00:21:41,690 --> 00:21:43,100
I put my name on an IOU for this money.

314
00:21:43,100 --> 00:21:44,360
You're paying it back.

315
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:47,380
H-How am I supposed to pay back 5,000?

316
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:48,870
They already agreed to let me go.

317
00:21:48,870 --> 00:21:50,330
Why did you have to butt in?

318
00:21:51,220 --> 00:21:52,970
I helped you, and now I'm in the wrong?

319
00:21:52,970 --> 00:21:54,000
All this misery, just because

320
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:55,100
I ate one bowl of your wontons.

321
00:21:55,100 --> 00:21:55,860
Exactly.

322
00:21:56,040 --> 00:21:57,390
Jinbao, this lover of yours

323
00:21:57,390 --> 00:21:59,320
is nothing compared to my Cang.

324
00:21:59,510 --> 00:22:00,750
I'm not her lover.

325
00:22:00,930 --> 00:22:01,910
I'm her photographer.

326
00:22:01,910 --> 00:22:02,910
If you're not her lover,

327
00:22:02,910 --> 00:22:04,760
then why did Jinbao
go to all that trouble to save you?

328
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:06,190
Men are all heartless.

329
00:22:06,220 --> 00:22:06,860
Agreed.

330
00:22:10,560 --> 00:22:11,560
Five thousand...

331
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:13,530
Dinner's ready!

332
00:22:17,560 --> 00:22:18,620
Alright, alright.

333
00:22:18,670 --> 00:22:19,760
Let's go eat first.

334
00:22:19,760 --> 00:22:21,080
How am I supposed to eat?

335
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:22,040
It's 5,000 yuan.

336
00:22:22,040 --> 00:22:23,360
How can I swallow anything after that?

337
00:22:23,360 --> 00:22:25,280
Six for luck! Five for top honors!

338
00:22:25,280 --> 00:22:26,040
Drink!

339
00:22:30,470 --> 00:22:31,150
Kailai,

340
00:22:32,190 --> 00:22:35,760
another toast—
may your youthful ambition never fade,

341
00:22:36,080 --> 00:22:39,340
and may you conquer all enemies
like a general from heaven.

342
00:22:39,360 --> 00:22:40,890
That sounds pretty heroic.

343
00:22:42,710 --> 00:22:43,340
Come on.

344
00:22:49,070 --> 00:22:50,280
Slow down.

345
00:22:51,240 --> 00:22:53,240
That damn Cang Guanglian,

346
00:22:53,470 --> 00:22:56,000
he promised to take care of my parents.

347
00:22:56,130 --> 00:22:57,700
That's why I became his.

348
00:23:00,950 --> 00:23:02,150
You promised me too.

349
00:23:03,280 --> 00:23:04,490
What did I promise you?

350
00:23:04,490 --> 00:23:06,150
You promised to pay back the money.

351
00:23:06,150 --> 00:23:08,110
If you can't, you'll have to marry me.

352
00:23:08,110 --> 00:23:09,110
Nonsense.

353
00:23:09,760 --> 00:23:10,520
Chen Kailai,

354
00:23:10,800 --> 00:23:12,310
you should have some conscience.

355
00:23:12,310 --> 00:23:13,230
I can testify.

356
00:23:14,510 --> 00:23:15,160
Come on, come on.

357
00:23:15,160 --> 00:23:16,290
Let's raise a glass.

358
00:23:16,870 --> 00:23:18,800
To Kailai for surviving an ordeal.

359
00:23:18,910 --> 00:23:19,840
Come on, come on.

360
00:23:20,080 --> 00:23:21,210
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

361
00:23:21,240 --> 00:23:22,440
To survive an ordeal.

362
00:23:33,930 --> 00:23:36,770
[Fulai Photo Studio]

363
00:23:54,910 --> 00:23:55,840
Master...

364
00:23:59,670 --> 00:24:00,710
What "Master"?

365
00:24:04,480 --> 00:24:05,590
You're drunk.

366
00:24:24,700 --> 00:24:25,760
The guy named Yu...

367
00:24:27,290 --> 00:24:28,460
you killed him.

368
00:24:29,700 --> 00:24:30,530
That certain?

369
00:24:42,530 --> 00:24:45,190
You wouldn't have suffered
if you'd given me up.

370
00:24:46,530 --> 00:24:47,660
Why didn't you?

371
00:24:53,290 --> 00:24:54,740
Because in Nanjing,

372
00:24:56,050 --> 00:24:58,710
you protected the common people
with your life.

373
00:25:02,770 --> 00:25:04,170
And you protected me too.

374
00:25:17,380 --> 00:25:19,270
Here you go. Your wontons.

375
00:25:20,090 --> 00:25:20,810
Enjoy.

376
00:25:21,700 --> 00:25:22,290
Sir,

377
00:25:22,900 --> 00:25:25,430
why is the Chunguang Photo Studio
sealed off?

378
00:25:28,180 --> 00:25:29,330
The Japanese did it.

379
00:25:29,540 --> 00:25:30,590
I heard the owner

380
00:25:31,070 --> 00:25:32,180
is a Communist.

381
00:25:32,680 --> 00:25:34,610
[Uncle Hai,
Underground Communist Party Member]

382
00:25:33,810 --> 00:25:34,740
Then where is he?

383
00:25:34,780 --> 00:25:35,530
Dead.

384
00:25:35,640 --> 00:25:36,700
He died on the spot.

385
00:25:37,050 --> 00:25:38,090
You didn't see it—

386
00:25:38,850 --> 00:25:39,780
it was so tragic.

387
00:25:41,330 --> 00:25:42,660
Please enjoy your meal.

388
00:26:09,610 --> 00:26:11,210
Broken Bridge gave his life.

389
00:26:27,260 --> 00:26:29,060
Then who exactly is Chen Kailai?

390
00:26:29,940 --> 00:26:32,000
He's just an ordinary photographer.

391
00:27:01,010 --> 00:27:02,490
Are you... Inspector Su?

392
00:27:04,540 --> 00:27:06,710
I'm Jin Meina
from the Telecommunications Section.

393
00:27:06,710 --> 00:27:08,020
Director Li is occupied with
official business,

394
00:27:08,020 --> 00:27:09,480
so he asked me to see to you.

395
00:27:43,290 --> 00:27:44,700
What a dump.

396
00:27:45,820 --> 00:27:47,100
They did it on purpose.

397
00:27:48,020 --> 00:27:49,910
At least we've made it into No. 76.

398
00:27:53,990 --> 00:27:56,450
When will Hoshino Eisei arrive
in Shanghai?

399
00:27:58,300 --> 00:27:59,700
Day after tomorrow, 8 AM.

400
00:28:06,100 --> 00:28:08,230
The Japanese want to end the war early.

401
00:28:09,950 --> 00:28:11,950
Project Slumber is their last hope.

402
00:28:13,300 --> 00:28:14,580
Dr. Hoshino

403
00:28:15,090 --> 00:28:16,280
is their trump card.

404
00:28:26,580 --> 00:28:28,230
He can be our trump card too.

405
00:28:38,990 --> 00:28:41,120
Next, we need to be more high-profile.

406
00:28:41,390 --> 00:28:43,260
We need to make sure all of Shanghai

407
00:28:43,260 --> 00:28:44,100
sees it.

408
00:29:01,670 --> 00:29:04,870
That night, you called me "Master."

409
00:29:06,340 --> 00:29:07,600
I called you "Master"?

410
00:29:08,340 --> 00:29:10,060
You need a master

411
00:29:10,670 --> 00:29:14,200
to teach you how to survive
and establish yourself in Shanghai.

412
00:29:14,740 --> 00:29:16,190
I know how to take photos.

413
00:29:16,580 --> 00:29:17,910
That's my skill.

414
00:29:18,430 --> 00:29:19,950
In these turbulent times,

415
00:29:19,980 --> 00:29:21,740
can a camera keep you alive?

416
00:29:23,500 --> 00:29:25,670
There's still a lot you need to learn.

417
00:29:25,670 --> 00:29:26,430
From now on,

418
00:29:26,780 --> 00:29:29,230
come to the bathhouse more often
and take a bath.

419
00:29:29,230 --> 00:29:30,430
Again with the baths?

420
00:29:31,430 --> 00:29:33,300
I almost lost my life last time.

421
00:29:33,390 --> 00:29:34,950
As long as you listen to me,

422
00:29:35,670 --> 00:29:37,300
you'll stay alive.

423
00:29:40,340 --> 00:29:41,800
You don't intend to remain

424
00:29:41,910 --> 00:29:44,100
just a photographer forever, do you?

425
00:30:02,260 --> 00:30:02,990
Chen Kailai.

426
00:30:15,870 --> 00:30:17,270
Do you still remember me?

427
00:30:19,100 --> 00:30:19,710
I do.

428
00:30:30,700 --> 00:30:32,430
Where is that pretty lady boss?

429
00:30:32,710 --> 00:30:33,640
You mean Jinbao?

430
00:30:34,060 --> 00:30:35,150
She just went out.

431
00:30:35,540 --> 00:30:37,270
Usually, I mind the shop alone.

432
00:30:40,740 --> 00:30:43,260
What made you come all the way to Shanghai
to open a studio?

433
00:30:43,260 --> 00:30:44,500
My master sent me.

434
00:30:49,670 --> 00:30:51,130
Then where is your master?

435
00:30:51,630 --> 00:30:52,430
He died.

436
00:30:56,500 --> 00:30:57,630
Right in front of me.

437
00:31:00,060 --> 00:31:01,060
I came to Shanghai

438
00:31:01,990 --> 00:31:03,230
just to finish

439
00:31:03,740 --> 00:31:05,270
what he never got to finish.

440
00:31:05,990 --> 00:31:07,320
Opening a photo studio?

441
00:31:08,950 --> 00:31:11,410
And waiting for the person
he wanted to meet.

442
00:31:14,470 --> 00:31:15,500
Did you meet them?

443
00:31:19,990 --> 00:31:22,300
I forgot the secret code last time.

444
00:31:24,990 --> 00:31:25,870
What code?

445
00:31:32,780 --> 00:31:33,500
She said,

446
00:31:34,630 --> 00:31:37,030
"Your camera is American-made, isn't it?"

447
00:31:37,470 --> 00:31:38,190
I said,

448
00:31:38,950 --> 00:31:40,550
"My camera is German-made."

449
00:31:43,230 --> 00:31:45,230
I heard there's color film now.

450
00:31:46,100 --> 00:31:46,710
Yes,

451
00:31:47,500 --> 00:31:49,740
but I still prefer black-and-white film.

452
00:31:49,740 --> 00:31:50,710
Black is black,

453
00:31:51,340 --> 00:31:52,400
and white is white.

454
00:31:56,150 --> 00:31:58,080
Then how could you forget the code?

455
00:31:59,020 --> 00:32:00,390
He died so suddenly

456
00:32:00,540 --> 00:32:01,600
and didn't tell me.

457
00:32:01,800 --> 00:32:03,250
I figured it out myself.

458
00:32:06,970 --> 00:32:08,910
You've thrown
the whole plan into disarray.

459
00:32:08,910 --> 00:32:11,040
The Organization will need to vet you.

460
00:32:12,600 --> 00:32:13,400
I understand.

461
00:32:18,950 --> 00:32:20,210
Hello, Broken Bridge.

462
00:32:20,950 --> 00:32:21,910
I'm Su Causeway.

463
00:32:29,340 --> 00:32:30,270
This is so great.

464
00:32:49,670 --> 00:32:52,020
These are what Li Musheng left behind.

465
00:32:52,020 --> 00:32:53,020
They're all here.

466
00:33:12,820 --> 00:33:14,340
Did he leave you any instructions?

467
00:33:14,340 --> 00:33:15,100
No.

468
00:33:15,820 --> 00:33:17,740
Everything happened so suddenly.

469
00:33:17,740 --> 00:33:20,070
I even had to guess
the secret code myself.

470
00:33:26,630 --> 00:33:27,780
Who is this woman?

471
00:33:28,390 --> 00:33:30,020
Why did Li Musheng copy all her letters

472
00:33:30,020 --> 00:33:31,190
into his notebook?

473
00:33:33,630 --> 00:33:34,540
You read them?

474
00:33:34,950 --> 00:33:36,300
I memorized every one.

475
00:33:39,060 --> 00:33:40,590
Then who do you think she is?

476
00:33:44,740 --> 00:33:45,630
A young woman

477
00:33:46,470 --> 00:33:47,330
from Shanghai.

478
00:33:48,340 --> 00:33:50,710
She lived in Tokyo for a while.

479
00:33:52,230 --> 00:33:54,670
She kept up correspondence with Li Musheng
the whole time,

480
00:33:54,670 --> 00:33:56,270
but they never actually met.

481
00:33:56,670 --> 00:33:58,870
She must've been a confidante of sorts.

482
00:34:01,670 --> 00:34:04,200
You figured all that out
from the letters too?

483
00:34:05,150 --> 00:34:07,210
He never mentioned this person to me.

484
00:34:10,659 --> 00:34:11,790
This was his secret.

485
00:34:14,500 --> 00:34:15,750
I was wondering why this old bachelor

486
00:34:15,750 --> 00:34:17,100
never got married.

487
00:34:17,830 --> 00:34:20,690
Turns out someone was
living in his heart all along.

488
00:34:22,020 --> 00:34:24,350
I always thought I knew him well.

489
00:34:25,020 --> 00:34:26,679
I even looked down on him a bit.

490
00:34:26,870 --> 00:34:27,800
I never imagined

491
00:34:27,989 --> 00:34:29,650
he was hiding so many secrets.

492
00:34:33,830 --> 00:34:35,060
How did you two meet?

493
00:34:36,219 --> 00:34:37,270
I met him in Nanjing

494
00:34:37,270 --> 00:34:39,219
when I was a war correspondent.

495
00:34:39,949 --> 00:34:41,949
He said he had a photo studio in Hangzhou

496
00:34:41,949 --> 00:34:42,750
and needed an assistant,

497
00:34:42,750 --> 00:34:43,659
so I went.

498
00:34:44,750 --> 00:34:46,880
Many of us went to Nanjing at that time.

499
00:34:47,659 --> 00:34:48,989
So your meeting

500
00:34:49,139 --> 00:34:50,540
wasn't really a coincidence.

501
00:34:50,540 --> 00:34:52,670
I always thought he was quite worldly.

502
00:34:53,219 --> 00:34:54,020
Turns out

503
00:34:54,310 --> 00:34:55,699
he was a Communist.

504
00:35:01,270 --> 00:35:02,530
Thank you for all this.

505
00:35:02,700 --> 00:35:04,350
You've been a great help to us.

506
00:35:04,350 --> 00:35:06,580
Is there anything else I can help with?

507
00:35:07,990 --> 00:35:08,700
No need.

508
00:35:09,310 --> 00:35:11,020
You've already done more than enough.

509
00:35:11,020 --> 00:35:11,950
This is it?

510
00:35:18,140 --> 00:35:18,870
Then...

511
00:35:19,310 --> 00:35:20,990
can I take a picture of you?

512
00:35:25,350 --> 00:35:25,990
Sure.

513
00:35:31,060 --> 00:35:32,830
What does this hold?

514
00:35:33,350 --> 00:35:35,100
All the beauty in the world.

515
00:35:35,390 --> 00:35:37,450
What is "all the beauty in the world"?

516
00:35:38,430 --> 00:35:39,560
I don't know either.

517
00:35:39,790 --> 00:35:41,500
Whatever it is, it's beautiful.

518
00:35:41,500 --> 00:35:43,430
But I'll definitely know someday.

519
00:35:44,660 --> 00:35:45,350
Ready?

520
00:35:45,700 --> 00:35:46,430
Look here.

521
00:35:48,430 --> 00:35:51,290
Do you still remember
what we said when we were kids?

522
00:35:53,020 --> 00:35:53,950
What is

523
00:35:54,470 --> 00:35:56,130
"all the beauty in the world"?

524
00:35:59,390 --> 00:36:00,470
Now I know.

525
00:36:02,660 --> 00:36:04,060
The most beautiful thing

526
00:36:04,870 --> 00:36:05,700
is peace.

527
00:36:10,060 --> 00:36:10,660
Look here.

528
00:36:25,990 --> 00:36:26,620
Will we...

529
00:36:27,470 --> 00:36:28,670
see each other again?

530
00:36:29,540 --> 00:36:30,270
I don't know.

531
00:36:31,430 --> 00:36:33,490
Then where can I find you if I need you?

532
00:36:34,290 --> 00:36:35,620
Just be a photographer.

533
00:36:42,790 --> 00:36:43,430
Goodbye.

534
00:37:16,310 --> 00:37:17,220
Inspector Su?

535
00:37:25,750 --> 00:37:26,680
What do you want?

536
00:37:27,270 --> 00:37:28,870
Get in. We'll talk in the car.

537
00:37:39,990 --> 00:37:40,950
How's business?

538
00:37:41,990 --> 00:37:42,700
Not so good.

539
00:37:44,470 --> 00:37:45,870
How about I find you a job?

540
00:37:46,390 --> 00:37:47,020
Sure.

541
00:37:49,390 --> 00:37:50,660
Be my photographer.

542
00:37:50,990 --> 00:37:51,660
No.

543
00:37:54,750 --> 00:37:56,470
There are plenty of photographers
in Shanghai—

544
00:37:56,470 --> 00:37:57,800
why does it have to be me?

545
00:37:58,520 --> 00:38:00,500
Because you make me look better in photos.

546
00:38:00,500 --> 00:38:01,960
Flattery won't work on me.

547
00:38:05,270 --> 00:38:06,660
Because I'm a traitor?

548
00:38:07,420 --> 00:38:08,750
You said that yourself.

549
00:38:10,520 --> 00:38:12,590
Are all you people at No. 76 like this?

550
00:38:13,020 --> 00:38:16,220
You ask me questions,
but you don't want to hear the truth.

551
00:38:25,960 --> 00:38:27,250
Why be a photographer?

552
00:38:28,140 --> 00:38:29,470
To make a living.

553
00:38:31,580 --> 00:38:32,180
That's it?

554
00:38:35,020 --> 00:38:37,310
And maybe take photos of things
that matter,

555
00:38:37,310 --> 00:38:38,390
to record this era.

556
00:38:41,470 --> 00:38:42,620
Taking photos of me

557
00:38:42,950 --> 00:38:45,950
is more meaningful
than working in a studio, isn't it?

558
00:38:45,950 --> 00:38:46,810
I don't see how.

559
00:38:50,620 --> 00:38:52,080
Just do it to make a living.

560
00:38:53,870 --> 00:38:54,910
I'm expensive.

561
00:38:57,220 --> 00:38:58,150
Name your price.

562
00:39:01,340 --> 00:39:02,380
Then...

563
00:39:03,140 --> 00:39:03,990
100 yuan a day?

564
00:39:03,990 --> 00:39:05,320
You've got a death wish?

565
00:39:05,350 --> 00:39:06,060
Deal.

566
00:39:08,950 --> 00:39:09,750
Are you sure?

567
00:39:11,990 --> 00:39:14,450
A car will come pick you up
tomorrow morning.

568
00:39:15,020 --> 00:39:16,540
I think that female pervert

569
00:39:16,540 --> 00:39:17,940
has taken a liking to you.

570
00:39:18,180 --> 00:39:19,100
How shameless.

571
00:39:19,750 --> 00:39:20,840
No way.

572
00:39:23,610 --> 00:39:24,650
Well,

573
00:39:25,020 --> 00:39:26,950
if only she weren't a traitor.

574
00:39:31,750 --> 00:39:33,140
You're even dreaming about her now?

575
00:39:33,140 --> 00:39:34,060
I'm telling you,

576
00:39:34,060 --> 00:39:34,990
if you dare to go,

577
00:39:34,990 --> 00:39:36,190
I'll break your legs.

578
00:39:37,060 --> 00:39:38,660
I don't want to go either.

579
00:39:39,100 --> 00:39:40,830
I just couldn't keep my mouth shut.

580
00:39:40,830 --> 00:39:43,090
I meant to scare her off
with a high price,

581
00:39:43,270 --> 00:39:44,390
but she agreed.

582
00:39:45,870 --> 00:39:47,270
Now you regret it?

583
00:39:47,660 --> 00:39:49,870
Here I am, the beautiful
dancing queen from Hangzhou—

584
00:39:49,870 --> 00:39:50,870
you wouldn't photograph me

585
00:39:50,870 --> 00:39:52,830
but insist on
photographing that she-devil.

586
00:39:52,830 --> 00:39:54,830
You think you've got lives to spare?

587
00:39:55,950 --> 00:39:58,100
That she-devil really is strange.

588
00:39:59,140 --> 00:40:00,430
You could say she's good,

589
00:40:00,430 --> 00:40:01,560
but she's a traitor.

590
00:40:01,910 --> 00:40:03,180
You could say she's bad,

591
00:40:03,180 --> 00:40:04,380
yet she saved my life.

592
00:40:05,180 --> 00:40:07,310
You didn't kill him in the first place.

593
00:40:07,750 --> 00:40:08,540
At most,

594
00:40:08,540 --> 00:40:10,470
she's got a bit of conscience left.

595
00:40:11,020 --> 00:40:12,910
Then why do you think
she specifically wants me

596
00:40:12,910 --> 00:40:14,310
to take her photographs?

597
00:40:15,580 --> 00:40:17,700
You just said you named a high price?

598
00:40:20,270 --> 00:40:21,470
How much did you name?

599
00:40:21,830 --> 00:40:23,020
More than you pay me.

600
00:40:23,870 --> 00:40:24,670
How much more?

601
00:40:28,700 --> 00:40:29,500
Ten yuan?

602
00:40:30,420 --> 00:40:31,770
One hundred yuan a day.

603
00:40:35,020 --> 00:40:35,910
Really?

604
00:40:36,470 --> 00:40:37,270
Are you sure

605
00:40:37,770 --> 00:40:39,570
she just wants you to take photos

606
00:40:39,580 --> 00:40:40,660
and nothing else?

607
00:40:42,350 --> 00:40:43,610
What are you thinking?

608
00:40:44,060 --> 00:40:45,190
Just taking photos.

609
00:40:45,870 --> 00:40:46,310
Go.

610
00:40:46,660 --> 00:40:47,790
You have to go.

611
00:40:48,390 --> 00:40:49,580
Even if you have to do something else,

612
00:40:49,580 --> 00:40:50,710
you still have to go.

613
00:40:51,180 --> 00:40:53,380
Now you don't mind that she's a traitor?

614
00:40:53,950 --> 00:40:54,750
She is.

615
00:40:54,790 --> 00:40:56,590
As long as you're not, it's fine.

616
00:40:56,850 --> 00:40:58,250
Come on, do the math.

617
00:40:59,020 --> 00:41:00,020
One hundred each time,

618
00:41:00,020 --> 00:41:01,680
and ten times is one thousand.

619
00:41:02,180 --> 00:41:04,580
You sure changed your tune pretty quickly.

620
00:41:04,830 --> 00:41:06,180
Have you forgotten how you cursed her out

621
00:41:06,180 --> 00:41:07,830
last time when you were drunk?

622
00:41:07,830 --> 00:41:09,560
A person has to keep their word.

623
00:41:09,750 --> 00:41:10,880
Once we name a price,

624
00:41:10,990 --> 00:41:12,390
we have to honor the deal.

625
00:41:12,620 --> 00:41:14,710
That's the basic principle
of doing business.

626
00:41:14,710 --> 00:41:15,430
Besides,

627
00:41:15,910 --> 00:41:17,100
if you back out now,

628
00:41:17,540 --> 00:41:19,620
do you think
that she-devil will let you off?

629
00:41:19,620 --> 00:41:22,660
What if she has you thrown back in there
to suffer again?

630
00:41:22,660 --> 00:41:24,500
The wound on your hand just healed—

631
00:41:24,500 --> 00:41:26,160
imagine how much that'd hurt.

632
00:41:27,020 --> 00:41:28,060
Money-grubber.

633
00:41:29,040 --> 00:41:29,870
Such a miser.

634
00:41:29,950 --> 00:41:31,480
Can you live without money?

635
00:41:32,140 --> 00:41:34,540
Still, we shouldn't
just care about money.

636
00:41:34,620 --> 00:41:37,430
This country needs
people with conviction to save it.

637
00:41:37,430 --> 00:41:38,270
You?

638
00:41:38,540 --> 00:41:40,470
Save the photo studio first, okay?

639
00:41:40,660 --> 00:41:42,390
You're hardly the one to save the country.

640
00:41:42,390 --> 00:41:43,750
I can't get through to you.

641
00:41:43,750 --> 00:41:44,700
Chen Kailai!

642
00:41:45,220 --> 00:41:46,880
You need to have a conscience!

643
00:41:47,270 --> 00:41:48,220
To save you,

644
00:41:48,220 --> 00:41:50,300
I borrowed money from Young Master Feng.

645
00:41:50,300 --> 00:41:51,560
Young Master Feng said

646
00:41:51,830 --> 00:41:52,890
if I don't pay him back,

647
00:41:52,890 --> 00:41:54,500
I'll have to marry into his family!

648
00:41:54,500 --> 00:41:55,630
That's a good thing.

649
00:41:55,880 --> 00:41:57,610
Young Master Feng is a good guy.

650
00:41:57,750 --> 00:41:58,750
Not marrying him!

651
00:41:59,020 --> 00:42:00,220
Marrying his father.

652
00:42:00,500 --> 00:42:01,500
He's already 80.

653
00:42:02,910 --> 00:42:03,700
Eighty?

654
00:42:04,270 --> 00:42:05,270
How's his health?

655
00:42:06,350 --> 00:42:07,480
Not good, of course.

656
00:42:08,220 --> 00:42:10,150
Then he doesn't have many years left.

657
00:42:10,150 --> 00:42:10,870
I think it's a good match.

658
00:42:10,870 --> 00:42:12,180
Just grit your teeth and get through it.

659
00:42:12,180 --> 00:42:13,640
Chen Kailai, you bastard!

660
00:42:13,960 --> 00:42:15,790
I haven't forgotten the money I owe you.

661
00:42:15,790 --> 00:42:17,000
What good does remembering it do?

662
00:42:17,000 --> 00:42:17,870
You have to pay it back!

663
00:42:17,870 --> 00:42:19,330
I will! I definitely will!

664
00:42:22,930 --> 00:42:26,100
[Hoshino, Japanese Medical Doctor]

665
00:42:37,410 --> 00:42:38,040
Ishida.

666
00:42:42,220 --> 00:42:43,420
It's been a long time.

667
00:42:44,150 --> 00:42:45,580
[Ishida,
Japanese Bacteriology Lab Technician]

668
00:42:48,430 --> 00:42:49,830
It's been a long journey.

669
00:42:50,380 --> 00:42:51,580
Welcome to Shanghai.

670
00:42:57,100 --> 00:42:57,870
Look here.

671
00:42:58,950 --> 00:42:59,790
Smile.

672
00:43:00,100 --> 00:43:01,540
Three, two...
